# collision.pdl - ship against land, in DIRECT flight (owner 2026-10-25). Re-read every 2 s, no rebuild.
# Design: BOOK 16.game/RPG-SPACE-COLLISION-AND-DESTRUCTION-DESIGN.md (same order as RPG Maker canPass: map limit, then ghost, then solid cells, then other entities).
# COLL | key | value | what it does
COLL | enabled       | 1   | 0 = the ship flies through the land (ghost)
COLL | block         | 1   | 1 = a move into the land is refused (the ship stays), 0 = only the damage happens
COLL | contact_alt   | -7  | ship altitude (state/direct_z.txt) at or below which the hull touches the land. CALIBRATED 2026-10-25 from the engine's own log: the planet surface is sunk 8 + altitude levels below the hull floor (capped 16), the hull hangs about 1 level under its floor, so it touches at about -7
COLL | ship_size     | 12  | the hull's footprint in cells (ship_01 size_x / size_y)
COLL | land_size     | 16  | the planet page in cells; hull [dox, dox+ship) against page [0, land) on both axes
COLL | crew_base_pm  | 5   | per-mille (1/1000) of max hp every crew member loses per hit (minimum 1 hp): very slight, it just registers the damage
COLL | crew_speed_pm | 5   | extra per-mille per speed step (1..4; faster moves hit harder)
